{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement. The context inputs `N`, `M`, and `X` are used only as sizes/predictors. All parameters (`beta`, `alpha`, and `sigma`) have exactly one built-in prior sampling statement before they are used in the likelihood.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N; // Number of observations
  int<lower=1> M; // Number of covariates
  matrix[N, M] X; // Design matrix
  vector[N] y;    // Observations
}

parameters {
  vector[M] beta;
  real alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}

model {
  // Weakly informative containment priors
  beta ~ normal(0, 10);
  alpha ~ normal(0, 2);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 2);

  // Observational model
  y ~ normal(X * beta + alpha, sigma);
}
